      "html": "† <big><span dir=\"rtl\">חִטָּה</span></big>  <strong>substantivo feminino: trigo (</strong>hebraico pós-bíblico <em>idem</em>, aramaico <span dir=\"rtl\">חִנְטִין</span>, <span dir=\"rtl\">חִיטְּתָא</span>, <span dir=\"rtl\">ܚܶܛܬܳܐ</span>; árabe <span dir=\"rtl\">حِنْطَةٌ</span> <strong>)</strong>;—absoluto <span dir=\"rtl\">ח׳</span> <a data-ref=\"Exodus 9:32\" href=\"/Exodus.9.32\">Ex 9:32</a> + 6 vezes; plural <span dir=\"rtl\">חִטִּים</span> <a data-ref=\"Genesis 30:14\" href=\"/Genesis.30.14\">Gn 30:14</a> + 20 vezes; <span dir=\"rtl\">חִטִּין</span> <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 4:9\" href=\"/Ezekiel.4.9\">Ez 4:9</a>; construto <span dir=\"rtl\">חִטֵּי</span> <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 27:17\" href=\"/Ezekiel.27.17\">Ez 27:17</a>;—<em>trigo</em>, singular principalmente poético, do trigo em crescimento <a data-ref=\"Exodus 9:32\" href=\"/Exodus.9.32\">Ex 9:32</a> (E), <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 8:8\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.8.8\">Dt 8:8</a> <a data-ref=\"Job 31:40\" href=\"/Job.31.40\">Jb 31:40</a>; <a data-ref=\"Joel 1:11\" href=\"/Joel.1.11\">Jo 1:11</a>; semeado <a data-ref=\"Isaiah 28:25\" href=\"/Isaiah.28.25\">Is 28:25</a>; produto alimentício <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 32:14\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.32.14\">Dt 32:14</a> (<span dir=\"rtl\">חֵלֶב כִּלְיוֹת ח׳</span> <em>gordura dos rins do trigo</em>, isto é, o mais seleto, ver <a data-ref=\"BDB, חֵ֫לֶב\" href=\"/BDB,_חֵ֫לֶב\", dir=\"rtl\">חֵלֶב</a>) <span dir=\"rtl\">חֵלֶב ח׳</span> <a data-ref=\"Psalms 81:17\" href=\"/Psalms.81.17\">ψ 81:17</a> (cf. <a data-ref=\"Psalms 147:14\" href=\"/Psalms.147.14\">147:14</a> abaixo); alhures plural; trigo semeado <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 12:13\" href=\"/Jeremiah.12.13\">Je 12:13</a>; <em>colheita de trigo</em> <span dir=\"rtl\">קְצִיר ח׳</span> <a data-ref=\"Genesis 30:14\" href=\"/Genesis.30.14\">Gn 30:14</a> (J), <a data-ref=\"Exodus 34:22\" href=\"/Exodus.34.22\">Ex 34:22</a> (JE), <a data-ref=\"Judges 15:1\" href=\"/Judges.15.1\">Ju 15:1</a> <a data-ref=\"I Samuel 6:13\" href=\"/I_Samuel.6.13\">1 S 6:13</a>; <a data-ref=\"I Samuel 12:17\" href=\"/I_Samuel.12.17\">12:17</a> <a data-ref=\"Ruth 2:23\" href=\"/Ruth.2.23\">Ru 2:23</a>, + <a data-ref=\"II Samuel 24:15\" href=\"/II_Samuel.24.15\">2 S 24:15</a>, onde inserir segundo 𝔊 We Dr; trigo debulhado <a data-ref=\"Judges 6:11\" href=\"/Judges.6.11\">Ju 6:11</a>; <a data-ref=\"I Chronicles 21:20\" href=\"/I_Chronicles.21.20\">1 Ch 21:20</a> cf. versículo <a data-ref=\"Judges 6:23\" href=\"/Judges.6.23\">23</a>; medido <a data-ref=\"I Kings 5:25\" href=\"/I_Kings.5.25\">1 K 5:25</a> = <a data-ref=\"II Chronicles 2:9\" href=\"/II_Chronicles.2.9\">2 Ch 2:9</a> (<span dir=\"rtl\">חטים מַכּוֹת</span>, ler <span dir=\"rtl\">ח׳ מַכֹּלֶת</span> como <a data-ref=\"I Kings 5:25\" href=\"/I_Kings.5.25\">1 K 5:25</a> = <em>trigo para alimento</em> Th Be Ke segundo as versões), versículo <a data-ref=\"I Kings 5:14\" href=\"/I_Kings.5.14\">14</a>; <a data-ref=\"I Chronicles 27:5\" href=\"/I_Chronicles.27.5\">27:5</a> <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 45:13\" href=\"/Ezekiel.45.13\">Ez 45:13</a>; armazenado (com cevada, azeite e mel) <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 41:8\" href=\"/Jeremiah.41.8\">Je 41:8</a>; para alimento <a data-ref=\"II Samuel 17:28\" href=\"/II_Samuel.17.28\">2 S 17:28</a>, <span dir=\"rtl\">חֵלֶב חִטִּים</span> <a data-ref=\"Psalms 147:14\" href=\"/Psalms.147.14\">ψ 147:14</a> (cf. <a data-ref=\"Psalms 81:14\" href=\"/Psalms.81.14\">81:14</a> acima); <span dir=\"rtl\">לֹקְחֵי חִטִּים</span> <a data-ref=\"II Samuel 4:6\" href=\"/II_Samuel.4.6\">2 S 4:6</a> (ler <span dir=\"rtl\">סֹקְלָה ח׳</span> 𝔊 We Dr); <span dir=\"rtl\">סֹלֶת ח׳</span> <em>flor de farinha de trigo</em> <a data-ref=\"Exodus 29:2\" href=\"/Exodus.29.2\">Ex 29:2</a> (P); <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 4:9\" href=\"/Ezekiel.4.9\">Ez 4:9</a> (<span dir=\"rtl\">חִטִּין</span>, plural aramaico) misturado com cevada, favas, lentilhas, etc., e transformado em pão.",
